{"name":"Elite Teal","hex":"#133337","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"elite","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of high birth or social position; aristocratic or patrician.","Representing the choicest or most select of a group."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A special group or social class of people who have a superior social or economic status and attendant power, advantages, or privileges in society; a member of such a group.","An individual member of such a group."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/elite"},{"term":"teal","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of various small freshwater ducks of the genus Anas that are brightly coloured and have short necks.","A dark, somewhat bluish-green colour; a dark cyan."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a bluish-green colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/teal"}],"entries":[{"title":"Elite","blocks":[{"text":"In political and sociological theory, the elite are a small group of powerful or wealthy people who hold a disproportionate amount of wealth, privilege, political power, or skill in a group. Defined by the Cambridge Dictionary, the \"elite\" are \"the richest, most powerful, best-educated, or best-trained group in a society\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e8/Prime_Minister_Boris_Johnson_UNGA_visit_%2851786182369%29.jpg/330px-Prime_Minister_Boris_Johnson_UNGA_visit_%2851786182369%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elite"},{"title":"Teal","blocks":[{"text":"Teal is a dark cyan color. Its name comes from that of a bird, the Eurasian teal which has a similarly colored stripe on its head. The word is often used colloquially to refer to shades of cyan in general."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/Smithsonian_-_NMAAHC_-_Teal_blue_dress_and_cropped_jacket_designed_by_Ann_Lowe-_